  "notes": "USAGE:\nAlmost exclusively used for negative things — problems, weaknesses, flaws, contradictions, or incompetence. Rarely if ever used for positive revelations. Common in news reports and formal analysis.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {問題|もんだい}が{露呈|ろてい}する (problems are exposed)\n- {弱点|じゃくてん}が{露呈|ろてい}する (weaknesses come to light)\n- {矛盾|むじゅん}が{露呈|ろてい}する (contradictions are revealed)\n- {限界|げんかい}が{露呈|ろてい}する (limitations are exposed)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {発覚|はっかく}する: to be discovered — for scandals or wrongdoing specifically\n- {暴露|ばくろ}する: to expose, to reveal — actively revealing secrets (transitive)",
